; HDA.EXE's description, for cargo drivers: it goes into the zip as
; HDA.INF (with Source= added) and into CATALOG.TXT as one line per
; [Devices] entry. Raise Version= for every change that is published.
; The kernel's built-in HD Audio driver, moved to user mode (FREEHOLD
; D-238). The built-in took any PCI audio device of subclass 03 (HD Audio);
; a catalog line matches vendor + base class, so the controllers' vendors
; are listed with the sound class, QEMU's two by their IDs, and HDA.EXE
; ends at once, saying so, on a multimedia device that is not HD Audio.
[Driver]
Name=HDA
Version=1.0.0-1
File=HDA.EXE
Description=Intel High Definition Audio
Licence=MIT
Basic=Yes

[Devices]
8086:2668 sound
8086:293E sound
8086:* sound
1002:* sound
1022:* sound
10DE:* sound
1106:* sound
1039:* sound
10B9:* sound
1D17:* sound
